I thought so too, and when I learned about it thought it counterintuitive,
was about to suggest a patch, and promptly shut up. Frankly, when I
thought about it, I didn't want it to work that way. Giving money to an
off-aligned priest will not have any effect upon your alignment, but
giving money to a co-aligned priest *will* improve it. 

The rationale is, I suppose, that priests are just too hard to find on a
regular basis; only two are guaranteed in the first thirty or so levels,
so saving the life of a priest of Loki is just a good idea no matter how
deeply you'd like your extra-large pet to eat him. And once you have
gotten all the armor bonuses you can out of the smug little reindeer-
eater, you're perfectly free to hammer on him a while (so long as you can
survive doing so).



